      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "35fa58e008899e8899142b9b5fbad220",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"appendix-the-recursiveimagewidget\">Appendix \u2014 the <code>RecursiveImageWidget</code></h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The rule-authoring widget, inlined as an anywidget. A <em>placement</em> is\n<code>[x, y, scale, angle_deg]</code>: the base box (world-width <code>BASE</code>, see the JS)\nscaled, rotated clockwise, centered at <code>(x, y)</code> in world coords <code>[0, 1]</code>.\nThe <code>parent</code> placement defines the base frame; each child in <code>children</code> is\nanother placement, and the recursive rule is the similarity mapping the\nparent box onto that child box.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
